    "title": "<p>Essential diagnostic criteria for uterine leiomyosarcoma</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Carlos Parra-Herran",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoTableGridLight\" style=\"background: #DAEEF3; border-collapse: collapse; border: none;\" border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 53.4pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 550.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 53.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"708\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Conventional (spindle cell) uterine leiomyosarcoma</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Two or more of the following:</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-indent: -18.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Marked cytological atypia (2+/3+ nuclear atypia)</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-indent: -18.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Tumour cell necrosis</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-indent: -18.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>&ge;&nbsp;4&nbsp;mitoses/mm<sup>2</sup> (equating to &ge;&nbsp;10&nbsp;mitoses/10&nbsp;HPF of 0.55&nbsp;mm in diameter and 0.24&nbsp;mm<sup>2</sup> in area)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 53.4pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 550.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 53.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"708\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Epithelioid uterine leiomyosarcoma</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">One or more of the following:</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-indent: -18.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Moderate to severe cytological atypia (2+/3+ atypia)</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-indent: -18.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Tumour cell necrosis</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-indent: -18.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>&ge;&nbsp;1.6 mitoses/mm<sup>2</sup> (equating to &ge;&nbsp;4&nbsp;mitoses/10&nbsp;HPF of 0.55&nbsp;mm in diameter and 0.24&nbsp;mm<sup>2</sup> in area)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 53.4pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 550.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 53.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"708\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Myxoid uterine leiomyosarcoma</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">One or more of the following:</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-indent: -18.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Moderate to severe cytological atypia (2+/3+ atypia)</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-indent: -18.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Tumour cell necrosis</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-indent: -18.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>&gt;&nbsp;0.4&nbsp;mitoses/mm<sup>2</sup> (equating to &gt;&nbsp;1&nbsp;mitosis/10&nbsp;HPF of 0.55&nbsp;mm in diameter and 0.24&nbsp;mm<sup>2</sup> in area)</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-indent: -18.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Infiltrative borders&nbsp;/ irregular margins</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>",
    "imageUrl": null,
    "thumbnail": null
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 36703,
    "bookid": 34,
    "chapterId": 242,
    "fileId": 13032,
    "type": "WSI",
    "diagnosis": "Conventional (spindle cell) leiomyosarcoma",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "The tumour is hypercellular and comprised of disorganized intersecting fascicles. Neoplastic cells are spindled and feature atypical hyperchromatic nuclei; pleomorphism is appreciated at low and mid magnifications. Mitotic activity exceeds 4 mitoses/mm<sup>2</sup> (equating to &gt; 10 mitoses/10 HPF of 0.55 mm in diameter and 0.24 mm2 in area) and includes atypical forms. Coagulative tumour cell necrosis is noted, characterized by a sharp interface between viable and non-viable tissue. Necrosis tends to occur in tumour areas away from large vessels (leaving a rim of viable tumour around vascular structures).",
    "source": "Carlos Parra-Herran",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/13032.dzi",
    "thumbnail": null
  },
  {
